Neomi · נעמי — Tunisian Kitchen
================================

Hebrew-first (RTL) restaurant site with a French translation, built to get
people to come and eat rather than to browse a catalogue.

Read CONTENT_TODO.md first — phone numbers, hours and address are real now;
the map coordinates are still unset.


Opening hours
-------------

Hours live in the database (BusinessHours), one row per weekday with two
service windows — Sun-Thu 13:00-16:00 and 18:00-22:00, Fri/Sat closed.

Editing DEFAULT_HOURS in seed_data.py does NOT change a database that
already has hours; that list only fills an empty table. Edit hours at
/admin/hours, or force the defaults with:

    python3 seed_data.py --reset-hours


Running it
----------

1. Open WSL.
2. cd "/mnt/c/Users/karen/OneDrive/מסמכים/Uri/neomi-restaurant"
3. python3 app.py
4. Open http://127.0.0.1:5000/

Admin is at /admin. Set the password with:

    python3 seed_data.py --set-admin-password

If port 5000 says "address already in use", an older server is still
running:  pkill -f "python3 app.py"

Auto-reload while editing Python or templates (never on a public server -
it exposes an interactive console to anyone who triggers an error):

    NEOMI_DEBUG=1 python3 app.py

Without NEOMI_DEBUG, Flask caches templates, so an edit to anything under
templates/ needs a restart before it shows up.


Serving it for real
-------------------

Flask's built-in server handles one request at a time and is not meant to
face the internet. In production use gunicorn, which ignores the
`if __name__ == '__main__'` block in app.py entirely:

    gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:$PORT --workers 2 app:app

Environment variables a host should set:

    NEOMI_SECRET_KEY        random string; keeps admin logins alive across
                            restarts and deploys
    NEOMI_ADMIN_PASSWORD    used by --set-admin-password where there is no
                            terminal to type into
    NEOMI_HTTPS=1           marks the session cookie Secure, so it is only
                            ever sent over HTTPS


Booking notifications
---------------------

The site sends no email at all - there is no mailbox, no SMTP settings and
no address published anywhere. A submitted table booking does two things: it
saves a row, and it hands the customer a pre-filled WhatsApp message to send
from their own phone.

The row is committed before the message is built, so a customer who closes
the tab without sending it still has a booking - it is just one that only
/admin/reservations knows about. That page is therefore the backstop worth
checking daily.

Read the message a customer would send, without waiting for a real one:

    python3 notify.py

Never set NEOMI_DEBUG on a public server.


Photos and video
----------------

Source photos live outside the repo, in ../photos. They are 2–3 MB PNGs,
iPhone HEICs and QuickTime videos — none of which is servable as-is.

    python3 tools/build_assets.py

converts everything into static/images/: photos become WebP at several
widths, and the two MP4s are re-encoded for the web. About 12 MB in total,
down from ~110 MB of camera originals. Re-run it whenever media is added or
replaced; the naming is driven by the IMAGES and VIDEOS manifests at the top
of that file.

The videos are re-encoded rather than copied, because the originals are shot
for archive (the gallery clip is 4K vertical at 26 Mbit/s). The hero loop
also has its audio stripped, since it plays muted behind the headline:

    hero-loop.mp4         5.6 MB -> 0.3 MB
    summer-at-neomi.mp4  42.4 MB -> 5.5 MB

This step needs ffmpeg. It uses a system one if installed, otherwise the
static build from the imageio-ffmpeg package in requirements.txt. Without
either, photos still build and the videos are skipped with a message.

The generated folders under static/images/ are committed, because the
source photos live outside the repo and the server has no way to rebuild
them. After re-running the build, commit the changed files too.


The menu
--------

seed_data.py is the transcription of the printed card (תפריט חדש 11.8) and
is the source of truth. Running it replaces all menu items:

    python3 seed_data.py

Useful flags:
    --reset-hours          overwrite opening hours with the defaults
    --set-admin-password   change the /admin password

Day-to-day menu edits are easier in /admin/menu, which now has separate
Hebrew and French name and description fields plus a sort order.

The PDF itself is served at /static/menu/neomi-menu.pdf and linked from the
menu page as a download.


Looking inside the database
---------------------------

The data lives in instance/restaurant.db (SQLite, one file). The standard
tool is the sqlite3 CLI:

    sudo apt install sqlite3
    sqlite3 instance/restaurant.db

If it is not installed, tools/db.py does the same job with no install:

    python3 tools/db.py                      interactive SQL prompt
    python3 tools/db.py tables               tables and row counts
    python3 tools/db.py show business_hours
    python3 tools/db.py "SELECT * FROM menu_item WHERE category='fish'"
    python3 tools/db.py --backup             timestamped copy before editing

Note the orders table is named "order", a reserved word - it has to be
quoted in SQL.


Layout of the code
------------------

    app.py                routes, language handling, asset-width lookup
    models.py             database models + MENU_CATEGORIES
    i18n.py               all Hebrew and French copy, in one place
    content.py            phone/address/social + gallery manifest
    notify.py             the WhatsApp booking hand-off
    seed_data.py          the printed menu, transcribed
    tools/build_assets.py photo library -> web assets
    tools/db.py           command-line access to the database
    templates/            base + one per page, plus admin/
    static/css/style.css  burgundy-and-gold theme taken from the logo

Adding or changing wording means editing i18n.py, not the templates.
